WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.380
So — you went and saw Suspiria.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.340
Maybe you even sat through the whole thing!

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.580
This two-and-a-half hour journey is definitely
not the sort of moviegoing experience that

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.260
goes down well for everybody.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.280
We're sure you have a few questions.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.020
Around Suspiria's midpoint, Madame Blanc,
the Markos Dance Company's top instructor,

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.920
begins to develop a new dance concept centering
around the theme of rebirth.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.280
By then, we're well aware that the company
is secretly a front for an ancient coven of

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.140
witches, who seem to be violently sacrificing
young dancers for nefarious reasons.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.540
While the details of Blanc's plan aren't made
totally explicit, her proposal heavily implies

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.640
that the dance will be used to resurrect the
coven's ailing leader, the witch called Mother

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.360
Markos.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.520
It also seems like the feat will require a
human sacrifice.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.320
It’s implied that the coven tried the ritual
before with the dancer Patricia, played by

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:54.329
Chloe Grace Moretz but something about the
ceremony went wrong, leaving Markos near death

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:56.300
and Patricia's whereabouts unknown.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.659
When audiences first meet Susie Bannion, played
by Dakota Johnson, she evokes a lot of sympathy.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.640
Her sheltered upbringing and self-taught dance
talents serve to make her a protagonist we

00:01:07.649 --> 00:01:12.170
can root for, and we spend most of the movie
scared about what's going to happen to her.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:16.570
The witches of the coven clearly regard her
as a sacrifice in the making, all but licking

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:20.620
their teeth at the idea of offering her up
as part of some deadly ritual.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.620
Of course, by the time we get to the end of
the movie… well, joke's on them, right?

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:30.380
Come to find out, Susie is actually a reborn
ancient witch by the name of Mother Suspiriorum,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:34.329
one of the oldest witches in existence, who
was central to the founding of the occult

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:35.329
company.

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:39.340
As Susie's staunchly-religious birth mother
later claims while on her death bed, Susie

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:42.740
is not a daughter that she loves, but instead
her greatest sin.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.799
It's a devastatingly mean thing to say about
one's child, but she's also kind of right.

00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:52.280
By the end of the movie, Susie is no babe
in the woods, but instead a force of ageless

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:56.530
power who is finally returning to life to
lead a league of witches — even if she's

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.740
not entirely aware of her identity when the
movie begins.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:05.520
While Patricia resisted the coven, Susie embraces
it, going from a newcomer to a leader in the

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.189
company with remarkable speed.

00:02:07.189 --> 00:02:12.190
But the mystery of what happened to Susie's
predecessor looms over the academy, with Patricia's

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:17.260
disappearance being investigated by fellow
student Sara as the movie revs up toward a

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.060
bloody climax.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:22.820
Minutes before a public dance performance,
Sara discovers that Patricia didn't disappear

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.560
from the academy at all.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.870
Instead, she's trapped inside it, somehow
still alive along with other victims of the

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.410
witches, including Olga the woman who was
literally torn apart by Susie's dancing.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:37.060
While the victims are all still alive, their
bodies are rotted and mangled.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.599
Thanks to some witchcraft, they are trapped
in a state of deathless suffering a devastating

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.040
fate which soon befalls Sara as well.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.860
The innocent dancers of the Markos company
aren't the only people being manipulated into

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.060
involvement in the witches' ritual.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.900
They also target Dr. Jozef Klemperer, Patricia’s
elderly therapist, plotting to bring him into

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.890
their rebirth ritual as an unwilling witness.

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:01.569
As we learn throughout the movie, the somber
therapist is haunted by the disappearance

00:03:01.569 --> 00:03:04.720
of his wife Anke, who vanished during World
War II.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.189
Klemperer has spent decades trying to move
on from this traumatic separation which makes

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:13.090
it all the more shocking when she appears
to him, seemingly back from the dead, at his

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:15.160
country home outside of Berlin.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.270
In an intriguing twist, she's played by actress
Jessica Harper, who played the role of Suzy

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.069
in the original Suspiria.

00:03:22.069 --> 00:03:26.450
Their reunion is so emotional that you almost
don't notice that Anke is walking Klemperer

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:31.480
from the countryside back into West Berlin,
right up to the doors of the Markos academy.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.680
As Klemperer realizes where his wife has led
him, she is suddenly revealed to be a cruel

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.460
illusion of the witches, leading him into
a trap.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.860
In the movie's final act, the characters all
descend on a hidden chamber inside the academy,

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:47.780
where the rebirthing ritual for Mother Markos
is set to take place.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:52.180
The company's students are there in a trance,
dancing and forming a sort of human altar

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.280
with their bodies.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:58.360
Klemperer's there among the witches as a captive
witness, and so is the guest of honor Mother

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:02.520
Markos herself, who appears in all her hideous
glory for the first time.

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:07.820
Since her last attempt at reincarnation, Markos
has been described as being on death’s door.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:12.739
Now we can see why it looks as though she
has become partially fused with another body,

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:16.260
with extra malformed limbs jutting impossibly
from bulbous form.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.350
But soon, it seems, she will be reborn in
a new body Susie's.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:24.701
As Susie enters the room to begin the ritual,
Markos and her allies believe the time for

00:04:24.701 --> 00:04:26.730
reincarnation has finally arrived.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:30.980
But while Susie is all confidence, Blanc is
uneasy, scared even.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.300
Something feels wrong to her.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.940
Susie isn't acting like the sheltered girl
we thought we knew — she's acting more like

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:38.060
she runs the place, putting Blanc on edge.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:43.380
Blanc tries to stop the ritual but fails when
Markos attacks her, nearly decapitating her

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.250
with telepathic magic, spraying blood everywhere.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:51.000
With Blanc sidelined, it seems like Markos’
resurrection is imminent.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.390
But it turns out that the ceremony isn't for
her rebirth at all.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:58.910
Instead, the ritual is the culmination of
a power play from an even stronger witch that’s

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:00.920
been brewing in the background the whole film.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:06.320
Tearing her flesh open, Susie reveals herself
to be none other than the revived Mother Suspiriorum

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:11.100
— the millennia-old entity who was a founding
member of the witches' occult order.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.630
Susie — or now Suspiriorum — begins to
unleash bloody hell on Markos and her allies

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.680
in the coven, who dared to seize power in
her place.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:23.840
She doesn't do it alone — instead, she summons
the living embodiment of Death itself to stroll

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:26.400
around the room making her enemy's heads explode.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:27.780
It's pretty trippy.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.700
After Markos and her followers are dispatched,
the rest of the movie is essentially Susie's

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.360
victory lap.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:37.700
She spares the lives of the dancers, as well
as the witches who weren't loyal to Mother

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:44.200
Markos, and also allows Patricia, Sara, and
Olga to finally die, their ruined bodies collapsing

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.460
to the ground in an act of motherly mercy.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:51.080
It's a completely different take on the original
Suspiria's story, and if the movie's cryptic

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.940
post-credits scene is to be believed, the
story might just be getting started.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:06:00.930
The original Suspiria, directed by Dario Argento
, had two sequels: Inferno and The Mother

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:04.880
of Tears, each focusing on a different one
of the powerful witches known as the Three

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:05.380
Mothers.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:10.120
Is it possible that the remake director Luca
Guadagnino is explicitly teasing sequels in

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.210
the vein of Argento's follow-ups?

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.680
While nothing's been announced yet, it is
possible.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:19.060
But don't worry too much about decoding that
cryptic last shot: according to screenwriter

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:24.150
David Kajganich, the brief scene of Susie
standing in the cold making vague gestures

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.240
wasn't even scripted.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:30.960
Most likely, the scene is just open to interpretation,
meant to send viewers out of the theater thinking,

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.960
talking, and weighing the ending's implications,
with a heavy sigh.

